\e[2J\e[2J\e[1;1HTest of known bugs in the DEC VT100 series. The numbering of some of\r\r\n
the bugs (A-F) refers to the article 'VT100 MAGIC' by Sami Tabih in\r\r\n
the 'Proceedings of the DEC Users Society' at St. Louis, Missouri, May\r\r\n
1983. To understand some of the tests, you have to look at the source\r\r\n
code or the article. Of course, a good VT100-compatible terminal\r\r\n
should not have these bugs (or have some means of disabling them)! If\r\r\n
a bug appears, you might want to RESET the terminal before continuing\r\r\n
the test. There is a test of the RESET function in the main menu.\r\r\n
\r\r\n
          Choose bug test number:\r\r\n
\e[9;1H\e[0J\r\r\n
